notify_lara:
  alias: Notify Lara (fan-out)
  description: "Single fan-out point for personal push notifications. Sends the same
    title/message to every device listed in the sequence below.\n\nWHY THIS EXISTS:
    adding or removing a device should be ONE edit here, not a hunt through every
    automation. Created 2026-08-10 when Lara wanted laundry alerts on her MacBook
    as well as her iPhone.\n\nTO ADD OR REMOVE A DEVICE: add or delete a step in the
    sequence. Available services as of 2026-08-10:\n  notify.mobile_app_iphone\n  notify.mobile_app_lara_s_15_macbook_air\n
    \ notify.mobile_app_laras_ipad_mini\n  notify.mobile_app_laras_mini_ipad\n\nNote
    the MacBook service is 'mobile_app_lara_s_15_macbook_air', NOT 'mobile_app_macbook_air'.\n\nDesign
    note: an earlier version used a templated `action: {{ repeat.item }}` over a target
    list, which failed to load. Explicit steps are used deliberately - do not re-clever
    this.\n\nUsed by: the four Laundry automations. Safe to reuse elsewhere - it carries
    no gating of its own, so callers keep their own vacation / in_bed conditions.\n\nmode:
    parallel so two alerts firing close together (washer and dryer finishing near
    each other) do not queue behind one another."
  fields:
    message:
      description: Notification body
      example: Cycle ran 52 min.
      required: true
      selector:
        text: {}
    title:
      description: Notification title
      example: Dryer finished
      required: true
      selector:
        text: {}
  icon: mdi:bell-ring-outline
  max: 10
  mode: parallel
  sequence:
  - action: notify.mobile_app_iphone
    alias: iPhone
    data:
      message: '{{ message }}'
      title: '{{ title }}'
  - action: notify.mobile_app_lara_s_15_macbook_air
    alias: MacBook Air
    data:
      message: '{{ message }}'
      title: '{{ title }}'
